Z||000000||Shaun41178||11-15-2000||05:10 PM||||I know that no Fieros came with a roller cam.  However did any of the aluminum head generation 2 engines have roller cams?  Like 89 Beretta's or early to mid 90's Luminas or something of that nature?  Or is the roller cam from GM strictly a Gen 3 cam?<P>I thought that some Gen 2 FWD cars had roller cams but I don't see any listings in my GM performance parts catalog.  Of course my book  is 3-4 years old so I don't have an updated book that might list gen 2 roller cams.  My comp cam book lists nothing either but that is old as well.<P>Ok if no Gen 2's came with a roller cam anyone know if it is possible to put in a Gen 3 roller cam and not have any problems with the intake manifold interfering or any other probs?<P>The reason I am asking is I am about to acquire a Gen 2 engine and am adapting the aluminum heads as well as my aluminum block to go in my Fiero and at the same time go to a roller cam if possible.  Someone please know or know where to direct me for info.  Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>2.8 With nitrous<BR>Soon to have a 3.2 with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Performance</A>||||reg||1
